module change-fedcir-practice-note-26.notes

/// Guidance binds the actors it names and moves only their priors
/// (docs/litigate/CHANGE.md §2.9): it prescribes nothing, and imposes no
/// duty on a party.
start waive-late-notice

terminal waived: "The late notice is excused"
terminal not-waived: "The late notice stands untimely"

/// Practice Note to Rule 26: "The court cannot waive the deadlines for
/// filing a notice of appeal or petition for review, even if the document
/// was deposited in the mail in a timely fashion."
chance waive-late-notice: "Court asked to waive a late notice of appeal" by court cite "Fed. Cir. R. 26"
{
  waive "Waives the deadline" -> waived p 0
  refuse "Refuses" -> not-waived p 1
}
